 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "tests whether they cover the vertices of ",
 StyleBox["targets", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"90b2001e-77d4-41e4-884d-81b731588059"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " covers a set ",
 StyleBox["T", "TI"],
 " at radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " when every ",
 StyleBox["t \[Element] T", "TI"],
 " has some ",
 StyleBox["c \[Element] s", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["d(t, c) \[LessEqual] r", "TI"],
 "; for ",
 StyleBox["T", "TI"],
 " the whole vertex set, ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " is an ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 "-dominating set."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4c04183a-e191-4905-8fe3-eab6480ab0f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A cover of every vertex at radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " is one at every larger radius, and a superset of a cover is a cover. The \
smallest covers are found by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindBallCover"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindBallCover", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fdd86c80-055e-4562-aece-54faba6ca5a9"],
 ", and their size is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DominationNumber"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DominationNumber", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "aea347f7-96d9-4b8a-a596-ff24def68d4a"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"58600212-2df9-45eb-94aa-3fae0c804479"]
}, Open  ]],

